<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Antoine of Vaudémont</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1400–1458</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Antoine of Lorraine, Count of Vaudémont</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Antoine of Vaudémont was count of Vaudémont and a member of the house of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorraine">Lorraine</a>. He claimed the Duchy of Lorraine against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rene-of-anjou">René of Anjou</a> and defeated and captured him at Bulgnéville in 1431. His son Ferry married René's daughter Yolande, and their son René II united Vaudémont with Lorraine.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/antoine-of-vaudemont.jpg" alt="Antoine of Vaudémont" width="320" height="173" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Odejea · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tombeau_d%27Antoine_de_Vaud%C3%A9mont.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
